Description: SecuBox Security Posture - honest board-truthful scorecard
 SecuBox Security Posture computes a single security score (mapped to a
 DEFCON 5-1 dial) from real, provenance-tracked signals collected over public
 sibling module sockets and unprivileged /proc reads.
 .
 Every indicator records where its value came from; signals that cannot be
 measured render as UNKNOWN or MANUAL and are excluded from the score rather
 than faked. Indicators are grouped by the six SecuBox module-domains
 (AUTH/WALL/BOOT/MIND/ROOT/MESH).
 .
 Features:
  * Overall posture score with DEFCON level and per-domain coverage
  * Repaired ANSSI CSPN compliance backbone (real checks, manual flagged)
  * Real TPN media-protection overlay (anti-piracy DNS, TLS coverage)
  * Actionable findings with remediation commands and module deep-links
  * Background 60s cache; read-only REST API on a unix socket
